    "rich_text_intro": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "text_intro": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Parboiled potatoes and burnished grapes wrap a border around an aromatic, stuffed trout. If you feel intimidated by cooking a whole fish, this is a great recipe to put that anxiety at ease &mdash; it is really just two moves: give the potatoes a head start so everything lands at once, then a flash under the broiler to blister the grapes.</p><p>The result is flawless fish alongside the most unexpected duo of grapes and potatoes. And the part nobody tells you about &mdash; getting a whole trout off the bone at the table &mdash; is three movements, which is further down the page.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
