      "settings": {
        "section_id": "off-the-bone",
        "liquid": "<style>\n  .sea-sheet {\n    --ink: #171717;\n    --muted: #5c5c5c;\n    --line: #e5e2dc;\n    --wash: #faf8f4;\n    --gold: #bb8f50;\n    color: var(--ink);\n    background: var(--wash);\n    border: 1px solid var(--line);\n    border-radius: 20px;\n    padding: 30px;\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__eyebrow {\n    font-size: 11px;\n    letter-spacing: .14em;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n    color: var(--gold);\n    font-weight: 600;\n    margin: 0 0 8px;\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__heading {\n    font-size: clamp(23px, 2.8vw, 30px);\n    line-height: 1.15;\n    font-weight: 600;\n    margin: 0 0 10px;\n    max-width: 22ch;\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__lede {\n    font-size: 15px;\n    line-height: 1.55;\n    color: var(--muted);\n    margin: 0 0 24px;\n    max-width: 68ch;\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__cols {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));\n    gap: 14px;\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__col {\n    background: #fff;\n    border: 1px solid var(--line);\n    border-radius: 14px;\n    padding: 18px;\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__col--pick {\n    border-color: var(--gold);\n    box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--gold);\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__num {\n    display: inline-flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: center;\n    width: 26px;\n    height: 26px;\n    border-radius: 50%;\n    background: var(--ink);\n    color: #fff;\n    font-size: 12px;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    margin: 0 0 10px;\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__col h3 {\n    font-size: 15.5px;\n    font-weight: 600;\n    line-height: 1.3;\n    margin: 0 0 7px;\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__col p {\n    font-size: 13.5px;\n    line-height: 1.55;\n    color: var(--muted);\n    margin: 0;\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__foot {\n    margin: 18px 0 0;\n    padding-top: 14px;\n    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);\n    font-size: 13px;\n    line-height: 1.55;\n    color: var(--muted);\n  }\n  @media (max-width: 749px) {\n    .sea-sheet {\n      padding: 22px;\n    }\n    .sea-sheet__cols {\n      grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n    }\n  }\n\n  .sea-sheet__fig {\n    margin: 22px auto 0;\n    max-width: 360px;\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__fig img {\n    width: 100%;\n    height: auto;\n    display: block;\n    border-radius: 16px;\n    box-shadow: 0 14px 34px -22px rgba(0,0,0,.5);\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__figcap {\n    margin: 10px auto 0;\n    max-width: 360px;\n    text-align: center;\n    font-size: 12.5px;\n    line-height: 1.5;\n    color: var(--muted);\n  }\n</style>\n<div class=\"sea-sheet\">\n  <p class=\"sea-sheet__eyebrow\">The part that actually intimidates people</p>\n  <h2 class=\"sea-sheet__heading\">Getting it off the bone is three movements.</h2>\n  <p class=\"sea-sheet__lede\">\n    Roasting a whole fish is easy. Serving one is where most people lose their nerve, and it is the\n    reason whole fish stays a restaurant order rather than a Tuesday. A cooked trout comes apart\n    along its own structure &mdash; you are not carving anything, you are unbuttoning it. Do this at\n    the table and it looks like a trick.\n  </p>\n\n  <div class=\"sea-sheet__cols\">\n    <div class=\"sea-sheet__col sea-sheet__col--pick\">\n      <span class=\"sea-sheet__num\">1</span>\n      <h3>Run a knife down the spine</h3>\n      <p>One shallow cut along the length of the backbone, from behind the head to the tail. You are\n      scoring a seam, not cutting through &mdash; the knife should stop when it meets bone.</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"sea-sheet__col\">\n      <span class=\"sea-sheet__num\">2</span>\n      <h3>Lift the top fillet away whole</h3>\n      <p>Slide the knife flat under the fillet and lift it off in one piece. It should come away\n      cleanly; the bones all run the other direction. Set it on a plate.</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"sea-sheet__col\">\n      <span class=\"sea-sheet__num\">3</span>\n      <h3>Pull the skeleton by the tail</h3>\n      <p>Take the tail end of the backbone and lift the whole frame up and away. The head comes with\n      it, the bottom fillet stays on the platter, and you are done.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <figure class=\"sea-sheet__fig\">\n    <img\n      src=\"{{ '20260825-Stetten-Wilson-228.jpg' | file_url }}&amp;width=760\"\n      alt=\"Whole roasted trout on a platter with potatoes and blistered grapes, seen from above\"\n      width=\"1200\"\n      height=\"1600\"\n      loading=\"lazy\"\n      decoding=\"async\">\n    <figcaption class=\"sea-sheet__figcap\">\n      Seen from above, the seam is obvious &mdash; the line running head to tail is exactly where the\n      knife goes.\n    </figcaption>\n  </figure>\n</div>\n",
        "padding_top": 24,
        "padding_bottom": 24,
        "divider": false,
        "narrow": false,
        "rounded": false,
